<title>INDIA: India's L&amp;T 1996/97 net seen 13 pct up.</title>
<headline>India's L&amp;T 1996/97 net seen 13 pct up.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Engineering and construction firm Larsen &amp; Toubro (L&amp;T) is expected to see its net profit improve 13.1 percent to 4.4 billion rupees in the year ended March 31, 1997, a Reuter poll showed.</p>
<p>Analysts at 28 leading securities and brokerage firms projected a low of 3.48 billion rupees and a high of 4.92 billion rupees against 3.88 billion a year ago.</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>LARSEN &amp; TOUBRO ----PAT seen up 13.1%, sales 20.99%</p>
<p>		     Net profit   1995/96    Net sales   1995/96</p>
<p>				(in million rupees)</p>
<p>Average		4,396.12  3,886.90    51,394.14  42,478.50</p>
<p>High		   4,918.70		  55,220.00</p>
<p>Low		    3,484.00		  43,571.00</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
